    <h3>The Module System</h3>
    <p>Everything in Metasploit is a <strong>module</strong> — a self-contained piece of Ruby code that performs a specific task. Modules are organized into categories:</p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Module Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>exploit/</td><td>Delivers a payload by taking advantage of a vulnerability</td><td>ms17_010_eternalblue</td></tr>
          <tr><td>payload/</td><td>Code that runs on the target after exploitation</td><td>windows/meterpreter/reverse_tcp</td></tr>
          <tr><td>auxiliary/</td><td>Scanning, fuzzing, brute-forcing, sniffing</td><td>scanner/smb/smb_version</td></tr>
          <tr><td>post/</td><td>Actions taken after gaining access</td><td>multi/recon/local_exploit_suggester</td></tr>
          <tr><td>encoder/</td><td>Transforms payload to evade detection</td><td>x86/shikata_ga_nai</td></tr>
          <tr><td>nop/</td><td>No-operation sleds for buffer overflow stability</td><td>x86/single_byte</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <div class="callout-title">💡 Analogy</div>
      <p>Think of modules like apps on your phone. Each app (module) does one job. The phone's operating system (Rex library + msfconsole) manages them all and lets them share resources like the network connection.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>The Database — Why It Matters</h3>
    <p>Metasploit connects to a <strong>PostgreSQL database</strong> to store everything it discovers: hosts, services, credentials, sessions, and notes. Without the database, results from one scan disappear when you close the tool. With it, you build a persistent picture of the target network across multiple sessions.</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-label">Shell — Starting the Database</div>
      <pre><span class="cmd">sudo systemctl start postgresql</span>   <span class="cmt"># Start PostgreSQL</span>
<span class="cmd">sudo msfdb init</span>                    <span class="cmt"># Initialize Metasploit DB</span>
<span class="cmd">msfconsole</span>                         <span class="cmt"># Launch framework</span>
<span class="cmd">db_status</span>                          <span class="cmt"># Verify: should say "Connected"</span></pre>
    </div>
