    <h3>Setting LHOST Correctly</h3>
    <p>A common beginner mistake is setting <span class="mono">LHOST</span> to a wrong or unreachable IP. <strong>LHOST is your machine's IP address</strong> — the IP that the target will call back to. Use the IP of your interface on the same network as the target.</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-label">Shell — Finding Your IP</div>
      <pre><span class="cmd">ip addr show eth0</span>    <span class="cmt"># Look for "inet" line — your IPv4 address</span>
<span class="cmd">ip addr show tun0</span>    <span class="cmt"># If using VPN (HackTheBox, TryHackMe)</span></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

